.TH GIT-PR-OPEN 1 "2026-06-14" "git-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-pr-open \- push a branch and create a pull request
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git pr-open
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git pr-open
pushes the current branch with upstream tracking and creates a GitHub pull
request without interactive prompts.
.PP
The command refuses dirty worktrees, refuses to open a pull request from the
base branch itself, and rejects a stale local base branch when it differs from
the exact remote base object ID.
.PP
GitHub pull request creation is pinned to the host and owner/repository derived
from the current checkout. Ambient GH_REPO and GH_HOST values cannot redirect
the operation. Structured default-branch discovery is pinned to the same
repository, so a foreign remote named origin cannot select the base. The base
fetch URL is validated against that repository, then the exact
refs/heads/base source is fetched without named-remote refspecs or tags. The
feature push target is resolved independently from branch push configuration;
fork heads are qualified as owner:branch.
.PP
The feature branch is pushed by immutable object ID through the captured
validated URL and the resulting remote object ID is verified. Upstream tracking
is installed locally only after the named remote is revalidated against that
URL. A concurrent remote configuration change aborts pull request creation with
a tracking-incomplete diagnostic after preserving the validated push.
.PP
The remote head is checked again immediately before creation. After creation,
the returned pull request is queried through structured output and must match
the requested repository, head and base refs, head repository,
cross-repository state, and exact head object ID. If a server-side race creates
an inconsistent pull request, the command reports its URL and exits nonzero.
.PP
Credential-bearing HTTP URLs, query or fragment suffixes, unsafe git-config key
bytes, and invalid GitHub owner or repository components are rejected before
exact transport helpers run. Normal SSH usernames remain supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-t, \-\-title " title
Pull request title. Required unless a
.B \-\-fill
mode is used.
.TP
.BI "\-b, \-\-body " body
Pull request body.
.TP
.BI "\-F, \-\-body-file " file
Read pull request body from file.
.TP
.BI "\-B, \-\-base " branch
Base branch. Defaults to the repository default branch.
.TP
.BI "\-H, \-\-head " branch
Head branch name for GitHub. Defaults to the current branch.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-draft
Create a draft pull request.
.TP
.BR \-\-fill ", " \-\-fill-first ", " \-\-fill-verbose
Use GitHub CLI commit-derived title and body modes.
.TP
.B \-\-no-maintainer-edit
Disable maintainer edits.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry-run
Print actions without changing anything.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Pull request was created, or dry-run completed.
.TP
.B 1
Pull request creation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or local environment error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-pr-checks (1),
.BR git-pr-ready (1)
